IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-disentitlement-deductions`

-- Tests of ei1-disentitlement-deductions.l4 (Act ss 18, 19, 20). Every expected value is written by hand from the
-- text of the section named beside the assertion; none is copied from the module's output. One #ASSERT per line.

§ `s 18(1)(a) capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment (src:449-450)`
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(a) the claimant was capable of and available for work and unable to obtain suitable employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) unable to work because of illness, injury or quarantine (src:451, 454)`
-- args: unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine; would otherwise be available; benefits are payable under any of sections 23 to 23.3
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(b) and s 18(2) the claimant was unable to work because of a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 18(1)(c) jury service (src:452)`
#ASSERT `s 18(1)(c) the claimant was engaged in jury service` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1)(c) the claimant was engaged in jury service` FALSE)

§ `s 18(1) entitlement for a working day (src:449)`
-- args: the day is a working day; proves (a); proves (b); proves (c)
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 18(1) the claimant is entitled to be paid benefits for the day as far as section 18 goes` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 19(1) earnings in the waiting period (src:458)`
-- args: the earnings in the waiting period; the amount the regulations prescribe be deducted
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` 300 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` 300 500 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` 300 200 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 19(1) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the first three weeks for which benefits are otherwise payable` 0 200 EQUALS 0

§ `s 19(2) earnings in any other week of unemployment (src:460-462)`
-- args: the earnings in the week; the weekly insurable earnings. With weekly insurable earnings of 500, 90% is 450:
-- 50% of earnings up to 450 and 100% of earnings above 450.
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 0 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 100 500 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 450 500 EQUALS 225
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 451 500 EQUALS 226
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 500 500 EQUALS 275
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 1000 500 EQUALS 775
-- rounding to the nearest dollar, the higher dollar when equidistant: 50% of 100.50 is 50.25; of 101 is 50.50
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 100.5 500 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 101 500 EQUALS 51
-- weekly insurable earnings of 333: 90% is 299.70, rounded to 300; earnings of 300.20 are 0.20 above it, which rounds to 0
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 300.2 333 EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable in the week` 301 333 EQUALS 151
-- the deduction cannot take the week's benefits below nothing
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the benefits payable in the week after the deduction` 300 275 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the benefits payable in the week after the deduction` 300 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 19(2) the benefits payable in the week after the deduction` 300 400 EQUALS 0

§ `s 19(3)(a) undeclared earnings (src:464-470)`
-- args: knowingly failed to declare (the Commission's opinion); the undeclared earnings; all s 19(2) amounts for the period; those applied to declared earnings
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` TRUE 400 275 150 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` FALSE 400 275 150 EQUALS 275
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` FALSE 400 150 150 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(a) the amount deducted from the benefits paid to the claimant for the period` FALSE 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§ `s 19(3)(b) spreading the deduction over consecutive weeks (src:471-473)`
-- args: the amount still to be deducted; the benefits paid for each consecutive week
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 400 (LIST 150, 150, 150, 150) EQUALS LIST 150, 150, 100
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 0 (LIST 150, 150) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 500 (LIST 100, 100) EQUALS LIST 100, 100
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 100 EMPTY EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 150 (LIST 150, 150) EQUALS LIST 150
#ASSERT `s 19(3)(b) the amount deducted in each consecutive week` 60 (LIST 150, 150) EQUALS LIST 60

§ `s 19(4) employment support measures and courses (src:475)`
-- args: earnings from employment under an employment support measure; that measure is one in 59(c) or (d); earnings or allowances for attending a course; the regulations provide for the deduction
#ASSERT NOT (`s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 19(4) the earnings or allowances may be deducted under section 19` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `s 20 days on which the claimant is not entitled (src:477, 479)`
-- args: the weekly rate of benefits; the number of working days. 1/5 of 405 is 81; of 402 is 80.40 (80); of 403 is 80.60 (81); of 402.50 is 80.50 (81, the higher dollar).
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` 405 2 EQUALS 162
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` 402 3 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` 403 1 EQUALS 81
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` 402.5 1 EQUALS 81
#ASSERT `s 20(1) the amount deducted for the excluded days in the waiting period` 405 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` 405 2 EQUALS 162
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` 402 3 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` 403 1 EQUALS 81
#ASSERT `s 20(2) the amount deducted for the days of disentitlement in a week that is not in the waiting period` 405 5 EQUALS 405
